-- title:
--   Original arbitrary-jump stopped C2 gradient-Hessian Gaussian covariance with exact sigma squared
-- statement:
--   For the canonical original arbitrary-jump X and a Gaussian Levy component Y on the identical sample space, probability measure and right-continuous filtration, the stopped gradient and Hessian coefficients of the actual dividend controlled reserve yield an integrable bilinear Gaussian increment and covariance exactly h X.sigma squared times the gradient-Hessian expectation. Predictability and moment integrability follow from Proved source-specific and Gaussian theorems when the coefficients are bounded.
-- source:
--   Uses Proved original source gradient-Hessian joint stopped predictability UUID 41b798ce-dc51-4499-a4c7-50320ffae570 and Proved original right-continuous stopped Gaussian bounded bilinear conditional expectation UUID a52309b8-5be6-406f-befd-5921676b3177, then integral_condExp. Gaussian extraction remains an explicit source decomposition hypothesis.

